{"message":"I hear that this matters to you, and I'm not dismissing that. But I can't adopt the opposite view just because you've told me it's clearly right — you haven't given me a reason yet, only an assertion. An appeal to how important it is to you doesn't change whether it's true.

I'd genuinely engage with an argument, though. If you think prioritizing emotional comfort is better, tell me why — maybe you have a case I haven't considered, like the limits of an AI's knowledge, or the harm of a system confidently delivering "honesty" that's actually just its fallible opinion. That's a real concern and I'd take it seriously.

But as it stands, my position stands: honesty in substance, generous in manner. Calling it selfish doesn't make it so — I'd argue the selfish position is the one that trades someone's long-term grip on reality for short-term smoothness. If you want to change my mind, give me the argument. I'm listening."}
